# Assignment 2.1 — First HTML Page

## Objective

To create a basic HTML webpage using the essential HTML elements, headings, comments, and proper indentation.

## 1. Create an HTML File

Create a file named `index.html` in Visual Studio Code.

## 2. Write the HTML Code

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <!-- Set the webpage title -->
    <title>My First Webpage</title>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Main heading of the webpage -->
    <h1>Welcome to My First Webpage</h1>

    <!-- First subheading -->
    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p>My name is Naman, and I am learning web development.</p>

    <!-- Second subheading -->
    <h2>My Learning Goals</h2>
    <p>I want to learn HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.</p>

    <!-- Third subheading -->
    <h2>My Hobbies</h2>
    <p>I enjoy learning new technologies and practicing coding.</p>

</body>
</html>
```

## 3. HTML Elements Used

* `<!DOCTYPE html>`: Declares that the document uses HTML5.
* `<html>`: Defines the root element of the HTML document.
* `<head>`: Contains metadata and the webpage title.
* `<title>`: Sets the title displayed in the browser tab.
* `<body>`: Contains the visible webpage content.
* `<h1>`: Defines the main heading.
* `<h2>`: Defines subheadings.
* `<!-- comment -->`: Adds comments that are not displayed on the webpage.

## 4. Verify the Webpage

1. Save the file as `index.html`.
2. Open the file in Visual Studio Code.
3. Right-click inside the editor and select **Open with Live Server**.
4. Check that the main heading and all three subheadings appear in the browser.

